<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to May 24.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to May 24.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to May 24 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week May 18- May 24</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,235,519 tns	127,908 tns    10.35 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	 779,282 tns	 88,633 tns    11.37 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,272,990 tns	139,135 tns    10.93 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to May 24</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    39,696,987 tns    4,288,688 tns    10.80 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    39,128,233 tns    4,270,254 tns    10.91 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    38,009,867 tns    4,061,033 tns    10.68 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 47 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 39 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 52 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
